    "absorbedVillageSourceId": "osm:node:1997440361",
    "newEvidence": "INP identifies Ladbech as a dispersed rural locality at site168.100 and locates Henchir el Guesirat168.099 within it. The latter converted point falls inside the separately tagged Castellum El Adbech ruins. Parliament publishes a2024 Health Ministry response naming the Adbech health center in Dkhilet Toujane.",
    "heldReason": "These sources support one named locality and distinguish its monument, but the two English residential fragments lack a shared addr:place/ref or enclosing named village footprint. Their individual membership in the third Arabic row remains inferred. Keep all three until that exact relationship is independently reviewed; do not require or invent a whole-locality polygon.",
    "parentCaveat": "The Arabic residential footprint crosses Beni Zelten515955 and Ain Tounine legacy516064 source boundaries; its current governorate-only context differs from the two English rows. No parent change is proposed."
